{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is running a cobbler-scaffold stitch task (#5361) to continue implementing `cmd/env` (the GNU `env` utility in Go). The task requires adding requirements R2.2, R2.3, R3.1, R3.2 from srd039-env to the existing implementation that already covers R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R2.1. Specifically:\n   - **R2.2**: `-u NAME` or `--unset=NAME` must remove variable NAME from environment before COMMAND runs. Multiple `-u` flags must be supported.\n   - **R2.3**: Each `NAME=VALUE` positional argument (before COMMAND) must set/override environment variables. First arg without `=` that isn't a flag starts COMMAND.\n   - **R3.1**: `-0` or `--null` must terminate output lines with NUL byte (0x00) instead of newline when printing environment (no COMMAND case).\n   - **R3.2**: When COMMAND is executed, env must exit with the same exit code as COMMAND.\n\n   Design decisions: extend existing code (don't rewrite R1.1-R2.1), use differential testing with `genv`, preserve all existing tests.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU reference `genv`\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Manual argument parsing (no cobra for this simple utility)\n   - Environment variable manipulation: inherit, clear (`-i`), unset (`-u`), override (`NAME=VALUE`)\n   - NUL-delimited output for safe parsing\n   - Exit code passthrough from child process\n   - `exec.LookPath` for command resolution, exit 127 for not found, 126 for permission denied\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd039-env.yaml**\n     - Full SRD with requirements R1-R4, goals G1-G4, acceptance criteria AC1-AC6\n     - Non-g