- Modify `cmd/env/main.go` to add:\n     - `-u NAME`/`--unset=NAME` flag parsing and environment variable removal (R2.2)\n     - `-0`/`--null` flag for NUL-delimited output (R3.1)\n     - Verify R2.3 and R3.2 are correctly handled (they appear to be already)\n   - Modify `cmd/env/env_test.go` to add differential tests for:\n     - `-u` single and multiple unset operations\n     - `--unset=NAME` long form\n     - `-0`/`--null` NUL-delimited output\n     - Combined flags (e.g., `-i -u NAME`)\n   - Run `go build ./cmd/env/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/env/` to verify no issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/env/ -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, env_test.go) and was about to begin implementation when the summary was requested. I had completed the analysis phase:\n   - R2.3 (NAME=VALUE) and R3.2 (exit code passthrough) already work in existing code\n   - R2.2 (`-u`/`--unset`) and R3.1 (`-0`/`--null`) need new code\n   - The flag parsing loop needs to handle `-u NAME` (flag with argument) and `-0` (simple flag)\n   - `buildEnv` needs an `unsets []string` parameter to filter out unset variables\n   - `printEnv` needs a `nullTerminated bool` parameter to use NUL vs newline\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the modified `cmd/env/main.go` with all changes in one pass, then write the modified `cmd/env/env_test.go` with new test cases, then build and test. The specific changes needed:\n   \n   For main.go:\n   - Add `nullTerm` bool and `unsets []string` variables alongside `ignoreEnv`\n   - Handle `-u NAME`, `--unset=NAME`, `-0`, `--null` in the flag parsing loop\n   - Update `parseShortFlags` to handle `'0'` and `'u'` (with `'u'` needing special handling for consuming next arg)\n   - Modify `buildEnv` to accept and apply unsets\n   - Modify `printEnv` to accept nullTerm and use `\\x00` vs `\\n`\n   \n   For env_test.go:\n   - Add test cases for: `-u HOME`, `--unset=HOME`