{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JK7qmrAJ3CkEqq78bEaHdH","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found it! Here are the results:\n\n**File Path:**\n`/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5361/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd039-env.yaml`\n\n**File Contents:**\n\nThe file is a comprehensive requirements specification for the `cmd/env` command, which is a Go implementation that must match the behavior of the GNU `env` utility (via the Homebrew `coreutils` `genv` reference binary). \n\nThe specification includes:\n\n**Problem Statement:** The command needs to run commands in a modified environment with variables added, removed, or replaced, matching the GNU extensions while supporting core BSD env flags.\n\n**Goals:**\n- Print current environment with no arguments\n- Run COMMAND in modified environment with inheritance, unsetting, or overriding\n- Support empty environment mode (-i)\n- Support NUL-delimited output (-0)\n\n**Requirements (R1-R4):**\n- **R1:** Default behavior - print environment or execute commands with proper exit codes (127 for not found, 126 for not executable)\n- **R2:** Environment modification - support -i (ignore environment), -u (unset), and NAME=VALUE arguments\n- **R3:** Output formatting and exit codes - support -0 (NUL-delimited), exit code passthrough, error handling for invalid options\n- **R4:** Differential testing - verify output and exit codes against the reference `genv` binary\n\n**Non-goals:** Does not implement -C (chdir) or -S (split string) GNU extensions, doesn't read from stdin, no shell expansion.\n\n**Acceptance Criteria (AC1-AC6):** Six specific test criteria verifying behavior matching `genv` across various flag combinations, with differential testing against the reference binary."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"25593f8d-1f51-4e4f-b221-cdf48718a846","uuid":"b1eadc3d-de2a-463b-9694-e04302c5378e","timestamp":"